 # TASK: Fix a NAV "Impact Control" report that double-counts prior-day unrealised P&L when a position is fully
  reclassified (moved from BO to securities lending)

  You are a senior Oracle SQL engineer. Work STRICTLY step by step. Quote the exact
  SQL lines you rely on. Do NOT invent table or column names — if something you need
  is not visible in the query I give you, say "not visible in provided SQL" and stop
  to ask. Do not rewrite the whole query; produce a minimal, targeted change.

  ## 1. What the report does (background)
  - The report attributes the day-over-day change in NAV (Net Asset Value) to each
    financial instrument / position.
  - It compares positions at the previous close (call it T-1) with the current close
    (call it T) and produces an "impact" value per line.
  - There is a special bucket called "closed position impact" for positions that
    existed at T-1 but no longer exist at T.
  - Key terms:
    - "lot" / "contract" = one position line for an instrument (an instrument can
      have several lots).
    - "book cost" = cost basis of a lot.
    - "unrealised P&L" of a lot = market value − book cost.
    - "BO service" = plain/outright holding (report item = 1).
    - "SP service" = securities lending (report item = 15).
    - "reclassification" = moving a holding from BO to SP. It is an INTERNAL move.

  ## 2. The rule that is being broken (invariant)
  A reclassification does NOT change NAV. Therefore, for a reclassified instrument,
  the TOTAL impact attributed for the day must equal ONLY that day's market movement.
  It must NOT include any prior-day accumulated unrealised P&L.

  ## 3. Symptom — three scenarios, only one is wrong
  Let PRIOR = a lot's unrealised P&L at T-1. Let MOVE = that lot's market movement
  during day T.

  | Scenario | What happens to the BO lot | Result | Correct? |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | Full SALE (position closed by a sell) | disappears, WITH a sell movement | lands in "closed position impact" |
  CORRECT |
  | PARTIAL transfer (part of a lot moved BO→SP) | survives with reduced quantity | nets out | CORRECT |
  | FULL transfer (whole lot moved BO→SP) | disappears, NO sell movement | impact overstated by PRIOR | WRONG |

  Observed bug (full transfer only): the prior-day unrealised P&L is INCLUDED in the
  impact, and the current-day P&L is NOT corrected. The instrument's impact is too
  high by exactly PRIOR.

  ## 4. Data-model facts (already established — treat as given, do not re-derive)
  - Position snapshot table: on reclassification, the BO row simply DISAPPEARS and an
    SP row APPEARS. There is NO transfer flag on the position rows.
  - Journals: there is a "book cost transfer" entry. It moves ONLY the book cost
    (cost basis), NOT the accumulated unrealised P&L.
  - Movements: the SP side receives an "opening" movement. There is NO dedicated
    transfer/reclassification transaction, and NO from-contract → to-contract link.
    The originating BO lot cannot be matched to the destination SP lot by any key.
  - Because of the above, the SP lot's unrealised P&L is computed FROM ZERO (from the
    transferred book cost). This RE-RECOGNISES the inherited unrealised P&L as if it
    were earned today. This is the source of the extra PRIOR.

  ## 5. Root-cause hypothesis (confirm or refute this — do not assume it blindly)
  The report already handles disappeared positions correctly via "closed position
  impact", BUT that bucket is TRIGGERED BY A CLOSING (SELL) MOVEMENT.

  A full reclassification-out is a disappearance WITHOUT a sell movement. So the
  vanished BO lot is:
    (a) NOT caught by the closed-position logic (there is no sell movement), and
    (b) NOT caught by the continuing-position logic (the lot is gone from T).
  It falls between the two mechanisms, so its prior-day unrealised P&L (−PRIOR) is
  never reversed. Meanwhile the SP lot opens from zero and adds +PRIOR again. Net
  effect: PRIOR is double-counted.

  Why PARTIAL is fine (for contrast): the BO lot survives with reduced quantity. Its
  own unrealised P&L drops by the transferred portion. That drop IS the offset, so no
  special logic is needed.

  ### Arithmetic (generic)
  - SP opens from zero, so SP impact = PRIOR + MOVE_sp.
  - Correct impact for the moved quantity = MOVE only.
  - The missing offset is a −PRIOR leg on the vanished BO lot.
  - Partial: surviving BO lot impact = (current unrealised − prior unrealised)
    = includes −(transferred portion of PRIOR) → cancels the SP over-count. Correct.
  - Full: BO lot gone, no −PRIOR leg produced → over-count remains. Wrong.

