  ## 7. THE FIX (apply only after the checklist confirms the hypothesis)
  Make the "disappeared position" detection SNAPSHOT-DRIVEN instead of
  sell-movement-driven:

    A lot that is present at T-1 and absent at T (matched at the granularity
    financial + contract + service) must contribute a closed/reversal leg equal to
    −(prior-day unrealised P&L), REGARDLESS of whether a sell movement exists.

  This routes a reclassification-out into the SAME "closed position impact" bucket
  that real sales already use, and it cancels the SP "from zero" over-count. No
  from→to link is needed.

  Two implementation options (pick the one that fits the existing structure with the
  smallest change):
  - Option A: change the T-1 ↔ T comparison to a FULL OUTER JOIN with
    COALESCE(<value>, 0) on BOTH sides, so T-1-only lots survive and produce their
    −PRIOR leg.
  - Option B: broaden the closed-position trigger predicate so it fires on the
    snapshot condition (present T-1 AND absent T), not only on a sell movement.

  ## 8. CRITICAL GUARDRAIL — do not double-count sales
  Real sales are ALREADY correct. Do NOT add a second closed-position leg on top of
  the existing sell-driven one. Make the trigger a SINGLE snapshot condition
  (present at T-1 AND absent at T) that covers BOTH sales and reclassifications, so
  any closed lot is counted EXACTLY ONCE.

